WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:08.140
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:08.140
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:13.440
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:13.440
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.820
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.820
the only thing I truly have

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.110
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.110
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:29.450
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:29.450
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:34.710
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:34.710
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:40.090
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:40.090
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:46.180
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:46.180
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:51.730
garakuta no yama kara

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:51.730
In the junk I've piled up,

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:55.810
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:55.810
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:01:01.110
hibike kono koe yo

00:00:55.810 --> 00:01:01.110
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:07.370
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:07.370
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:13.040
namida kareru made

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:13.040
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.090
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.090
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:23.420
namida hareru made

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:23.420
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:28.430
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:28.430
though I may lose my way,

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:32.270
egakikake no ima

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:32.270
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.770
kizamu

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:39.520
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.060
akashi

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.520
kono te de

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:45.350
Weak Point

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:45.350
Weak Point

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:51.020
With the game tied at three, the Hornets go on the offensive in the bottom of the ninth.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:55.670
A single run will let the Hornets walk away with the win,

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.650
and it's Mike Murdoch at bat!

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.150
He's been magnificent today, getting a hit in every at-bat.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.610
Will he be able to end the game?

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.250
Did you like that, Keene?

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.250
A win to celebrate your return.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.920
We turned the game around, and it was our fourth consecutive win.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.960
Fourth!

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.260
Murdoch's doing all the work.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.340
You didn't get a hit in any of your four at-bats.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:25.930
Shut up!

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:30.560
I gotta say, I don't feel like we can lose anymore.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.600
Yeah.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.020
We're closing in on the leading team too.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:39.110
Not to mention, Shigeno's pitching tomorrow.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.190
Let's keep up the pace and get our fifth consecutive win.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.780
Yeah, leave it to me.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.370
It's fine to be confident,

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:48.370
but the Salmons are different this year.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:51.290
They're usually ranked low,

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:56.540
but this season they've been fighting for the top spot in the West Division.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.540
Oh, you're well informed.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:02.010
Oh yeah, you played in the west until just recently.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:07.430
Well, just don't forget that they're a strong team.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.140
That sounds like fun.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.220
Fun?

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:10.910
Yeah.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.330
I was on the Salmons before.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.440
Knowing that I'll be playing my old teammates, I can't help getting fired up.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.280
I'll show Sanchez and Bolton how much I've improved.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.990
Don't forget that they've improved too.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:34.790
Just as Murdoch said, the Salmons aren't an easy opponent this year.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.420
How so?

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:42.420
Sanchez, Bolton, and the other veterans are leading the younger players to form a balanced team.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.880
This year the Salmons are especially good at winning close games.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.600
That's probably because of the Japanese duo who joined last year.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:52.770
Japanese duo?

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.100
Yeah.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.650
The closer, Onodera, has a great ERA of .820.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:04.940
Sakaguchi, the leadoff hitter, gets on base often and runs pretty fast.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:06.530
We should approach them with caution.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.640
Sakaguchi, huh?

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:17.540
In the bottom of the twelfth, the Salmons start their offense with their leadoff hitter.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.460
Sakaguchi steps into the batter's box with an OBP of nearly .400 this season.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.380
Play!

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.350
Safe!

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:39.600
Safe!

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.450
Safe! Safe!

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.120
Game over!

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.620
That's the eighth comeback for the Salmons this season!

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.330
They're back on top in the western division!

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.550
That was a big win we picked up.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:05.090
Yeah.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.970
Now it's all about keeping the lead.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:14.390
This two-game series with the Hornets is going to be the cornerstone for all future games.

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:17.730
The Hornets won again today for their fourth consecutive win.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.020
Oh, they're doing well.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:23.650
They'll pick up even more momentum unless we stop them early on.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:25.320
Yeah.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:29.860
A young team is hard to handle when they're in the zone.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.700
So, who's their starting pitcher for our first game?

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.620
According to their rotation, it's Shigeno.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.620
A match against Shigeno...

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.840
I can finally get him back for the World Cup.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.760
Hey, there, don't get too excited.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:53.010
We're more than familiar with Shigeno's personality.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:56.180
We gotta use that to our advantage, right?

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:59.140
Yeah, you bet.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.810
Tomorrow, we'll show him the hardships of the majors.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:04.610
Yeah.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:07.360
Sounds like an interesting conversation.

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:09.900
How about you let me in on it?

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.240
I'm sure I can help.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.910
Hey, they're all at it.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.080
I'm gonna go give them a quick welcome.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:34.840
Fox.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:39.140
I didn't know he made it to the majors.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.270
Long time no see, Fox.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.880
Hey, wait a minute!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:49.650
You don't have to ignore me just because we're playing today.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:53.320
I wanted to congratulate you on making it to the majors.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:56.030
You're interrupting my warm-up!

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.170
Go away!

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:01.450
What's his problem?

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:04.120
He's so cold to an old friend.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:07.670
Yo!

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:09.000
Old man Sanchez!

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.050
Have you been well?

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:12.550
Get this, Fox was—

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.960
Who do you think I am?

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:19.430
Don't come talk to me when you're just a rookie.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:23.810
Wh-What the hell?

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.100
I just came to say hello.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.080
Hey!

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:29.770
Hey, old man Bolton!

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:31.980
Stop loitering around on our side of the field.

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:33.150
You're an eyesore.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:38.740
You think you're a big boy now just because you've been playing well lately?

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:42.100
Get off your high horse, you baby rookie.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:45.500
Wh-What did you say?

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.840
Yo, you guys are doing well lately.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:50.460
Sakaguchi.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:52.590
It's been a while, Nelson.

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:55.090
I heard you're batting second for the Hornets.

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:58.010
That's some promotion for you.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.970
Well, I hope you won't be too hard on us today.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.430
See ya.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:12.480
The two-game series with the Salmons, the top team in the west, begins today.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:15.820
The Hornets are currently ranked second in the Central Division.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:20.200
Let's try to put some pressure on the Coyotes with some more wins in this series.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:24.780
Shigeno's pitches are looking especially fast today.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.870
We're sure to win again today.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:37.800
Man, those guys are really acting cold.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:41.640
I'll shut them out and make them regret their attitude.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:43.390
Play ball!

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:50.230
Strike!

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:54.650
Well, your pitches are as fast as they say.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.360
Foul!

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:03.030
Man, stop hitting like a wimp!

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.980
Just strike out already!

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.170
Safe!

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:25.740
It's pointless to make those fouls!

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:27.020
Ball!

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.140
Safe!

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.730
He let the runner just steal like that!

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.110
Calm down, Shigeno.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:38.860
First base!

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:41.780
Out!

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:45.120
Strike out!

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:49.560
Ball.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:50.890
Ball.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:52.310
Ball!

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:54.750
Ball!

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.420
Ball four!

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:57.130
Damn it.

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:57.750
Time out.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.880
Nice, you're getting angry.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:03.220
What's wrong?

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.510
Why are you so upset?

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:07.010
Calm down a bit.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:09.180
Who's upset?

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.310
Don't worry, just go back.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:14.020
Play!

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.110
Man...

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:19.320
You're all annoying like a swarm of flies!

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:21.860
Strike!

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:22.700
Out!

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:26.720
Nice shoulder.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.580
You're pitching too fast for the start of the game.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.370
Control your pitches and throw a little—

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:34.670
Don't worry!

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.300
I could throw for a million innings today.

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:41.720
Now hitting, number 2: Roy!

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:47.100
Old man Sanchez needs a few pitches to warm up!

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.970
Hit it before you get him started!

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:52.480
An easy pitch.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:55.810
Nice!

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:56.940
Good going, Roy!

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.360
Follow him, Nelson!

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:01.110
Ball!

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:02.940
Ball.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:04.700
Ball two!

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:05.360
Damn.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.580
You won't be able to make the starting line-up as long as I exist.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.080
You better give up, Nelson.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:22.050
Don't take me for a fool!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:27.970
Out!

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:30.100
Damn it!

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.850
What are you doing?

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:35.850
You flied an easy pitch from a 0-2 count!

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:40.150
Nelson used to be on the same team as Sakaguchi.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:46.910
They fought over starting line-up positions, and he was traded to the Hornets when he lost.

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:50.580
His anger must have resurfaced after meeting up again.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:53.450
Like I care about that.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:56.120
He wasn't good enough, and that's his problem.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:59.170
In fact, he should play better today to prove himself.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:10.140
Ball.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:11.720
Ball four!

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:13.680
Take that!

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:16.890
That's for being cocky before the game!

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:18.270
Damn.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.610
My breaking balls aren't going where I want them to.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:24.650
I'd like to change pitching patterns.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.450
I have an idea.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:37.190
Play!

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:43.400
Well, he can't throw any strikes, so let's not rush a hit.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.420
Strike!

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:48.510
Right down the middle?

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:53.140
Going with fastballs since you can't throw anything else?

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.770
Strike!

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:01.980
What are you swinging at that pitch for?

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.440
Focus on the ball!

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.240
Ball!

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:09.740
That catcher's good.

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:13.620
He changed the first pitch to a fastball right down the middle.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:18.250
It makes you think they changed their strategy to pitching fastballs,

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.750
but then they pitch two breaking balls in a row.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:25.000
He's utilizing the lack of control so that you won't know what they'll pitch.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.130
Strike out!

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:32.930
He couldn't have hit that.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:35.760
They threw two breaking balls low and outside.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:40.270
That high, inside fastball strike must have felt really close to his body.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:42.810
I see.

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:47.730
They were acting snotty before the game out of confidence.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:07.170
Out!

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:08.590
Aw, man!

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:10.510
We couldn't score again.

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:14.590
Sanchez has been pitching perfectly since the second inning.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:16.680
It's going to be tough to score off him.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:19.390
Your batting is just way too simple.

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:21.890
Can't you get some fouls or something?

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:25.650
Man, you're all just blindly swinging your bats.

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:35.010
Take this!

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:38.950
Damn it.

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:45.130
His pitches have slowed down.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.290
This is when we attack.

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.170
Yeah.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:52.760
He's probably too hot-headed to think about managing his strength anymore.

00:14:58.220 --> 00:14:58.850
Out!

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:03.560
Ball!

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:04.640
Ball four!

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:05.900
Damn it!

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:09.440
Hey, don't tell me you can't throw anymore.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:14.360
Out!

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.580
Ball! Ball four!

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:25.710
You're awfully tired, Shigeno.

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.420
No, I'm not.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:28.840
I'm switching you out.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:30.800
Leave the rest to the relief pitchers.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:32.550
Look, I'm fine!

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.590
Not today, you're not.

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:35.630
What?

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:39.300
Your pitches have no strength and terrible control.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:42.970
Not to mention you've been upset since the first inning.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:46.140
The fourth batter, Bolton, is up next.

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:50.150
If he hits big, we're going to have a tough time winning this game.

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:53.940
Who's going to let him hit big?

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:57.530
You better keep the jokes to just your hair.

00:15:57.530 --> 00:16:00.490
I struck out Bolton in the World Cup!

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:03.160
It's a lot better if I keep pitching!

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.370
Hey, calm down!

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:07.290
Look, I'll definitely get him out!

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:12.000
I can't leave the mound before old man Sanchez.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:14.710
Fine.

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:18.050
But if you can't hold him down here, you're going out.

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:20.260
Sure, fine by me!

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:24.970
He's still pitching?

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:27.190
Well, I expected that much.

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:30.400
He wouldn't back down in this situation.

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:34.110
Finish him, Bolton.

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:35.280
Play!

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:38.360
He's gonna get a hit off me?

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:42.470
Don't underestimate me, you seaweed head!

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:55.880
Calm down, Shigeno.

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:57.420
Throw one to the outside.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:59.050
Shut up.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.550
Just like in the World Cup,

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:06.660
I'll strike you out!

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:12.000
This forkball is what I was waiting for!

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:31.050
Darn, that didn't go all the way.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:33.250
Time out!

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.630
They're switching him out.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.090
That's too bad.

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:41.010
If they had kept him on the field for a few more batters, we could've taken the lead.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.890
So much for having an attitude, Shigeno.

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:50.520
Now we're back to square one thanks to him.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:54.810
Out!

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.870
Hey, good work.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:07.950
You pitched well, so wipe that frown off your face.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:10.540
There's nothing good about giving up a hit.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:11.410
You making fun of me?

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:14.540
Is that what you say when I'm trying to cheer you up?

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:16.790
You've been a real ass lately.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.960
What was that?

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.510
Say that again!

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:23.010
Hey, stop!

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:24.140
We're in the middle of a game.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:27.930
Geez, don't pick a fight. Let's be mature.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:31.730
Like you're one to talk when you haven't had a single hit.

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:33.480
Wh-What was that?

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.040
Look, stop!

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.900
Stop what?

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:38.320
I'm just stating the facts.

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:40.150
Hey, James.

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:41.950
You're starting this inning.

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.820
Oh, right.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:47.120
I totally forgot because I had to deal with these morons.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:51.830
Out!

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:53.540
Wow, what a waste.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:55.210
That pitch went right down the middle.

00:18:55.210 --> 00:19:00.550
I thought you'd hit it big after making fun of my batting.

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:05.720
Out!

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:08.970
Strike!

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:11.890
That bastard...

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:12.680
He's looking down on me.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.890
I'll definitely hit this one.

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:15.940
Hey.

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:18.650
I heard you used to be on the same team as Sakaguchi.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:25.240
Strike!

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:29.370
You should've swung at that pitch.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:33.710
Foul!

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:38.330
No wonder you got kicked off your last team.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.050
Damn it.

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:47.570
I can't let these guys...

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:50.050
make a fool out of me!

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.850
Okay, I got it!

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:54.520
Out!

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:57.190
Sorry.

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:58.020
It's fine.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:58.900
Don't worry about it.

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.230
Hey, Nelson.

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:03.900
You seem to have some history with Sakaguchi,

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.700
but stop being so tense out there!

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:07.990
Do you really wanna win?

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:10.490
Wh-What was that?

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:12.700
You're one to talk, Shigeno.

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:15.460
What?

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:18.670
You concentrated solely on your old teammates and self-destructed.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:21.340
If you're going to complain about others' play,

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:24.630
do a proper job as a professional first.

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:28.780
Don't mind him, Nelson.

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:29.300
Let's go.

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:29.990
Yeah.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:38.810
What is he doing?

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:40.690
You suck!

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.360
Go back to the minors!

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:44.780
Say that again!

00:20:58.500 --> 00:20:59.960
Strike out!

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.630
Game over!

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:06.340
A painful loss for the Hornets with a score of 6-3!

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:17.140
We lost because of me?

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:18.270
You kidding me?

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:21.100
You didn't do anything today either!

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:23.480
Yeah, I didn't make an error like you.

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:26.280
You haven't had a hit for several games now.

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:28.780
Are you a spy from some other team?

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:29.990
What was that?

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:31.490
You can't hit or field!

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:33.990
You're just a good-for-nothing on this team!

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:36.870
Why don't you stop talking big and practice a little?

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:39.290
You're just luggage to the Hornets.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:41.650
Now you've said it.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:43.540
Go to hell!

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:44.670
Hey, stop, you two!

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:46.550
Man, shut up.

00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:49.920
Neither of you guys did anything,

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:52.050
yet you're fighting about the game?

00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:53.720
What are you saying?

00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:57.850
We lost today because of your selfish plays!

00:21:57.850 --> 00:21:59.350
What was that?

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:01.600
You have no right to say anything!

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:04.190
Same goes for you!

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:06.650
You pick a fight over everything you don't like!

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:08.030
Hey, stop!

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:10.070
That's because your plays are nothing but jokes!

00:22:10.070 --> 00:22:11.200
That's enough!

00:22:12.530 --> 00:22:16.780
You're all just blindly blaming someone else.

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:19.000
Hearing you argue makes me sick.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:21.580
It's not one person's fault we lost.

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:28.460
Why don't you reflect on your own plays before you force your sins on someone else?

00:22:34.390 --> 00:22:37.300
How I'll hold the team together, huh?

00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:51.860
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:51.860
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:58.580
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:58.580
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.790 --> 00:23:00.250
yume wo

00:22:58.790 --> 00:23:03.420
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:03.420
oikaketeiru

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:06.210
ground no ue ni

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:09.420
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:09.420
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:13.390
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:13.390
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:14.050 --> 00:23:20.810
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:14.050 --> 00:23:20.810
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:28.110
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:28.110
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:32.860
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:35.880
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:35.880
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:38.490
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:43.540
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.250
kizukazu ni

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:43.540
suki ni natta

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:45.830
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:50.670
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:45.830 --> 00:23:50.670
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:53.260
zutto mae kara

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:58.350
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:55.140
otagai ni

00:23:55.140 --> 00:23:58.350
hikareteita

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:00.560
kono kimochi wa

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:07.560
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:07.560
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:15.670
Preview

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:15.670
Preview

00:24:11.670 --> 00:24:13.010
We can't win anymore!

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:14.840
The team's in complete disarray.

00:24:15.290 --> 00:24:18.930
I'll get the team back up to snuff with my pitching!

00:24:19.260 --> 00:24:21.990
Hey, that should've been a strike!

00:24:21.990 --> 00:24:25.330
Next time, on Major: A Resolute Will.

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:27.620
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:29.870
Next Time

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:29.870
Next Time

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:29.870
A Resolute Will

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:29.870
A Resolute Will
